To solve this problem, we need to determine the number of tiles that the painter robot will paint to color the kitchen floor for both the left and right grids provided. The robot starts at a border tile (xs, ys) facing one of the four diagonal directions and will eventually consume 7 units of black paint on his way until he stops at tile number 6. For the right grid, it will get stuck in a loop and consume 11 units of black paint, while for the left grid, it will stop painting after the robot consumes 7 units of black paint. For the other combinations of the input, the robot will never stop painting and therefore you don't need to calculate. 

